{"strongs": "H4519", "word": "מְנַשֶּׁה", "translit": "me.nash.sheh", "root": "מנשה", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine person and tribe", "gloss": "Manasseh", "definition": "מְנַשֶּׁה 136 proper name, masculine person and tribe Manasseh (interpretation of Gen 41:51 as Pi`el causative √II. נשׁה q. v.); — ׳ מ Gen 46:20 +; מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה Gen 41:51 + (on Judg 18:30 see משֶׁה ); with article (strangely), ׳ הַמְֿ Josh 1:12 + 10 t. (see below); ᵐ5 Μαν ( ν ) ασση ; — 1. \\ \\ a. Manasseh , eldest son of Joseph Gen 41:51 ; Gen 48:1 ; Gen 48:13 ; Gen 48:14 (twice in verse); Gen 48:17 ; Gen 48:20 (twice in verse), also Gen 50:23 (father of Machir; all E ), Gen 46:20 ; Gen 48:5 (both P ). \\ \\ b. of tribe, often + Ephraim (see אֶפְרַיִם ): (I) the part west of Jordan: a. ׳ בְּנֵי מ Josh 16:9 ; Josh 17:2 a ( ׳ בנימֿ הַנּוֺתָרִים ), v Josh 17:2 b; v Josh 17:6 v Josh 17:12 (all J E ), 1Chr 7:29 ; 1Chr 9:3 ( ׳ בְּנֵי אֶפְרַיִם וּמ ; Josh 13:29 see below); β. ׳ מ alone, Josh 17:5 ; Josh 17:8 (twice in verse); Josh 17:9 b; Josh 17:11 ; Josh 17:17 ; Deut 34:2 ( ׳ אֶרֶץ אֶפְרַיִם וּמ ; all J E ), 2Chr 30:10 ( id. ), Josh 16:4 ; Josh 17:7 ; Josh 17:10 (all P ), also apparently Deut 33:17 (poem), Judg 1:27 ; Judg 6:15 ; Judg 6:35 ; Judg 7:23 ; Isa 9:20 (twice in verse); Ps 80:3 + 10 t. Chronicles; γ. ׳ מַטֵּה מ 1Chr 6:55 ׳ חֲצִי מַטֵּה מ Josh 21:6 ; Josh 21:25 ; 1Chr 12:32 ( van d. H v. 1Chr 12:31 ); ׳ מַחֲצִית מַטֵּה חֲצִי מ 1Chr 6:46 (but on text see Kit ); וְאֶפְרַיִם ׳ שְׁנֵי מַטּוֺת מ Josh 14:4 ( P ); δ. ׳ חֲצִי שֵׁבֶט מ 1Chr 27:20 with article ׳ הַשֵּׁבֶט הַמְֿ Josh 13:7 ( D ). (2) of Manasseh east of Jordan; α. ׳ בְּנֵי מ Josh 22:30 ; Josh 22:31 ( P ); β. ׳ מ alone, Judg 11:29 (distinctly of territory), Judg 12:4 (but on text see GFM ), Ps 60:9 = Ps 108:9 ׳ חֲצִי הַמ 1Chr 27:21 γ. ׳ מַטֵּה מ Josh 17:1 a Josh 20:8 (both P ), 1Chr 6:47 ׳ חֲצִי מַטֵּה מ Josh 22:1 ( D ), Num 34:14 ; Josh 21:5 ; Josh 21:27 (all P ), 1Chr 6:56 חֲצִי מַטֵּה ׳ בְּנֵי מ Josh 13:29 ( P ); δ. ׳ חֲצִי שֵׁבֶט מ Deut 3:13 ( D ), Josh 13:29 ; Josh 22:13 ; Josh 22:15 (all P ), 1Chr 15:18 ; 1Chr 15:23 ; 1Chr 15:26 ; 1Chr 12:38 ( van d. H v. 1Chr 12:37 ); בֶּןיֿוֺסֵף ׳ חֲצִי שֵׁבֶט מ Num 32:33 ( P ); with article ׳ חֲצִי שֵׁבֶט הַמְֿ Josh 1:12 ; Josh 4:12 ; Josh 12:6 ; Josh 18:7 ; Josh 22:1 ; Josh 22:7 (all D ), Josh 22:9 ; Josh 22:10 ; Josh 22:11 ; Josh 22:21 (all P ). Here belong also (chiefly) references to ׳ מ as father of Machir (compare Gen 50:23 above): Num 27:1 ; Num 32:39 ; Num 32:40 ; Num 36:1 ; Josh 13:31 ; Josh 17:1 ; Josh 17:3 (all P ), 1Chr 7:14 ; 1Chr 7:17 and of Jair Deut 3:14 ( D ), Num 32:41 ( P ), 1Kgs 4:13 (compare מָכִיר , יָאִיר ). (3) of undivided tribe (never ׳ שֵׁבֶט מ ): α. ׳ בְּנֵי מ Num 1:34 ; Num 2:20 ; Num 7:54 ; Num 26:29 ; Num 36:12 (all P ); β. ׳ מ alone, Num 1:10 ; Num 26:28 ; Num 26:34 ; Num 27:1 b (all P ), Ezek 48:4 ; Ezek 48:5 γ. ׳ מַטֵּה מ Num 1:35 ; Num 2:20 ; Num 13:11 , ׳ מַטֵּה בְּנֵי מ Num 10:23 ; Num 34:13 (all P ). 2. son of Hezekiah, and king of Judah (Assyrian Menasê, Minsê Schr COT 2Kgs 21:1 ); — 2Kgs 20:21 ; 2Kgs 21:1 + 9 t. Kings, 12 t. Chronicles, Jer 15:4 . 3. two who had taken strange wives: \\ \\ a. Ezra 10:30 . \\ \\ b. Ezra 10:33 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4731')\">BDB4731</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4519')\">H4519</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4730')\">BDB4730</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4732')\">BDB4732</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מְנַשֶּׁה</bdbheb><sub>136</sub> <b>proper name, masculine person and tribe</b> <highlightword>Manasseh</highlightword> (interpretation of <ref ref=\"Gen 41:51\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"51\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"51\" onclick=\"bcv(1,41,51)\">Gen 41:51</ref> as Pi`el causative √II. <bdbheb>נשׁה</bdbheb> q. v.); — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 46:20\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(1,46,20)\">Gen 46:20</ref> +; <bdbheb>מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 41:51\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"51\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"51\" onclick=\"bcv(1,41,51)\">Gen 41:51</ref> + (on <ref ref=\"Judg 18:30\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(7,18,30)\">Judg 18:30</ref> see <bdbheb>משֶׁה</bdbheb>); with article (strangely), <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַמְֿ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 1:12\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(6,1,12)\">Josh 1:12</ref> + 10 t. (see below); <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Μαν</grk>(<grk>ν</grk>)<grk>ασση</grk>; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> <highlight>Manasseh</highlight>, eldest son of Joseph <ref ref=\"Gen 41:51\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"51\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"51\" onclick=\"bcv(1,41,51)\">Gen 41:51</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 48:1\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,1)\">Gen 48:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 48:13\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,13)\">Gen 48:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 48:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,14)\">Gen 48:14</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Gen 48:17\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,17)\">Gen 48:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 48:20\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,20)\">Gen 48:20</ref> (twice in verse), also <ref ref=\"Gen 50:23\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(1,50,23)\">Gen 50:23</ref> (father of Machir; all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Gen 46:20\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(1,46,20)\">Gen 46:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 48:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,48,5)\">Gen 48:5</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> of tribe, often + Ephraim (see  <bdbheb><reflink>אֶפְרַיִם</reflink></bdbheb>): (I) the part west of Jordan: <highlight>a.</highlight> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בְּנֵי מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 16:9\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(6,16,9)\">Josh 16:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 17:2\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,2)\">Josh 17:2</ref>a (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בנימֿ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>הַנּוֺתָרִים</bdbheb>), v<ref ref=\"Josh 17:2\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,2)\">Josh 17:2</ref> b; v<ref ref=\"Josh 17:6\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,6)\">Josh 17:6</ref> v<ref ref=\"Josh 17:12\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,12)\">Josh 17:12</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"1Chr 7:29\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(13,7,29)\">1Chr 7:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 9:3\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(13,9,3)\">1Chr 9:3</ref> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בְּנֵי אֶפְרַיִם וּמ</bdbheb>; <ref ref=\"Josh 13:29\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(6,13,29)\">Josh 13:29</ref> see below); <grk>β.</grk> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מ</bdbheb> alone, <ref ref=\"Josh 17:5\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,5)\">Josh 17:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 17:8\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,8)\">Josh 17:8</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Josh 17:9\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,9)\">Josh 17:9</ref>b; <ref ref=\"Josh 17:11